  "result": "Perfect! The dashboard function is working correctly. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Dashboard Function Summary\n\n**Location:** `src/reports.js`\n\n**Function signature:**\n```javascript\ndashboard(invoices, asOf) \u2192 { counts, outstanding, overdue, topCustomers }\n```\n\n**Features:**\n\n1. **counts** - Invoices per status:\n   - `draft`: Draft invoices (not sent)\n   - `issued`: Issued invoices with no payments\n   - `partially_paid`: Invoices with partial payments\n   - `paid`: Fully paid invoices\n\n2. **outstanding** - Total amount still due:\n   - Only counts `issued` and `partially_paid` invoices\n   - Calculated using `balanceDue()` for each invoice\n\n3. **overdue** - Object with overdue metrics:\n   - `count`: Number of overdue invoices (from `overdueInvoices()`)\n   - `amount`: Total amount due on overdue invoices\n\n4. **topCustomers** - Top 3 customers by outstanding balance:\n   - Aggregates multiple invoices per customer\n   - Sorted highest-to-lowest by amount due\n   - Excludes customers with no outstanding balance\n   - Returns fewer than 3 if fewer customers have outstanding\n\n**Test coverage (11 new tests):**\n- Empty invoices list\n- Status counting\n- Outstanding amount calculation\n- Overdue metrics\n- Top customers identification\n- Multiple invoices per customer\n- Partial payments handling\n- Draft invoice handling\n\n**All 390 tests pass** (379 previous + 11 new dashboard tests).",
